[{:seon.task/name "every-error-is-built-by-its-constructor"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by data's keys-schemas sweep, 2026-11-12: six error types are built as literal maps with :seon.error/type, never through `seon.contract/error`, so nothing checks them against their schema entry (the class seon.contract-test/every-error-type-a-raise-site-names-is-registered closed for the constructor's callers): :seon.lib/load-refused and :seon.lib/sysmem-refused (`seon.lib/sysmem`, `seon.lib/load-average`), :seon.render.value/insufficient-floor-budget-error and :seon.render.value/charge-exceeded (seon.print.select), :seon.task/refused (`seon.task/invalid`), :seon.fork-server/not-single-threaded. The fix: each site calls seon.contract/error, and a law refuses a map literal holding :seon.error/type outside seon.contract (read from the forms' :form/keywords and their text, proportional to the changed forms). Each type has its entry (bf87652eac)."
