  :seon.task/plan "The owner, 2026-11-03, on the bug-class audit read at c200a44aa9: \"make sure all of this fixes are applied and the docs are updated\"; by docs/merging.md#a-landing-message-carries-its-audit its report says what allowed the class, why the change makes it impossible, and which siblings it checked. What exists: contracts are armed everywhere, but what they say is loose: of about 1,780 :malli/schema in src about 125 answer :any and 151 answer :map, about 460 take a bare :map; :seon.error/base and entity-fact maps are open, so any extra key with any value passes. The change: a var property {:seon/boundary true}, starting with the edge functions of docs/failure-points.md, the store writers and the wire (server/answer, web/ui-call, model/sse-reply, model/request-body, repl/record!, my.root/load-example!); a boundary takes and answers named keyed schemas, no bare :map, :any or host object; bin/check contracts reports the count of loose returns and arguments with a ratchet that may only fall; maps the system writes are closed ({:closed true} on entity facts and error variants; [:map-of :keyword :seon.db/plain] where extension is wanted; agents' own schemas stay open); each tagged kind has one checked constructor (not built: seon.render/as [k v], planned in seon.render/a-render-tag-is-a-checked-schema; today :seon.render/as is only the output-kind option key). The rule is written in docs/checks.md#contracts-armed-at-definition and docs/decisions.md, with the owner's words. The cost bounds are settled first by seon.contract/a-contract-is-checked-once-and-costs-nothing."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.render/a-render-tag-is-a-checked-schema" "seon.contract/a-contract-is-checked-once-and-costs-nothing"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.contract-test/a-loose-boundary-is-counted}}
